title: GraphR1Viewing
tags: graph
---
// The story graph of route 1 as puzzle chapters (openspec/changes/story-graph). Graph
// nodes are data and never run. The game reads this file (src/story/graph.rs) and plays
// by it; dialogue_graph draws graphs/story_route1.dot and one graphs/box_<ID>.dot per box.
//   <<box ID "LABEL" [kind=chapter|hub|side|retry|stub] [goal=...] [parent=BOX] [entry=NODE]>>
//                                               entry: the Yarn node that enters the box. It runs
//                                               <<enter_box ID>>. A box without a scene has none
//   <<gate ID "LABEL" [detail=...] REQ...>>     a step or puzzle the player does
//   <<item ID "LABEL" REQ...>>                  an item the player gets
//   <<clue ID "LABEL" REQ...>>                  something learned; later boxes need it as BOX.ID
//   <<choice ID "LABEL" REQ...>> and <<option CHOICE ID "LABEL">>
//   <<exit ID "LABEL" REQ... to=BOX>>           a door out of the box
//   <<done BOX ID>>                             in a scene (not here): it performs that step, so the
//                                               graph draws it as written. ID: a gate, item, clue, option or exit id.
//                                               Doing an exit enters the box it leads to (its entry node runs)
// Scenes ask the graph with can("BOX", "ID") (BOX is the current box, the step is not done and
// its requirements hold; for an option also: no option of its choice is done) and
// is_done("BOX", "ID").
// A REQ is a node id (all needed), a|b (any one), choice=option, or BOX.clue: a clue
// from an earlier box. The player remembers it and the game never stores it, so it is
// a hint drawn in the diagrams, not a requirement the checks enforce. A node with no
// requirement in its own box follows the box's entry.
<<box R1Viewing "The viewing" goal="Get the flat" entry=Route1Start>>
<<gate knock "Knock on 3B: she shows him in">>
<<clue father "Her father owns the house" knock>>
<<gate window "Look at the window" knock>>
<<gate kitchen "Look at the kitchenette" knock>>
<<gate bath "Look at the bathroom" knock>>
<<exit flat "Tell her he's seen enough" window kitchen bath to=R1MoveIn>>
===
title: GraphR1MoveIn
tags: graph
---
<<box R1MoveIn "Moving in" goal="Get your keys and move in" entry=Route1MoveInStart>>
<<gate keys "Knock on 3A: the keys">>
<<item socks "Blush socks" keys>>
<<clue ask "“I'll ask” about the socks" keys>>
<<clue spare "She keeps the spare key" keys>>
<<gate carry "Carry his box up" keys>>
<<gate stow "Put the socks somewhere" detail="the drawers, or back in the box" carry socks>>
<<gate rules "Answer her knock: her rules" carry>>
<<clue shoes "Her rule: shoes off at her door" rules>>
<<clue answer "Her rule: if she knocks, he answers" rules>>
<<exit bed "Go to bed" stow rules to=R1Breakfast>>
===
title: GraphR1Breakfast
tags: graph
---
<<box R1Breakfast "Breakfast" goal="Bring her breakfast" entry=Route1SundayStart>>
<<gate text "Read her text">>
<<item bag "Bakery bag, back from the bakery">>
<<gate wear "Put the blush socks on" detail="she said she'd ask" R1MoveIn.ask>>
<<gate door "Knock on 3A with the bakery bag" detail="are you wearing them?" text bag R1MoveIn.shoes>>
<<exit bed "Go back to bed" door to=R1Free1>>
